  "body": "Complete source-bound native FP16 AWQ GEMM certificates for the independent AMD wave64 adaptation.\n\nFour complete source exports and rechecks prove initialized launch execution, actual whole-trace race freedom, output extraction and independent dense exact-real matrix-product equality. The universal theorem retains both native K16 MFMA passes, all K32 iterations, guarded FP32-to-half stores, the original fuel and supported shape bounds.\n\nThe source-only archive freezes 83 owned Lean modules and the SDK/reader. Independent rebuild without Git or owned compiled objects reproduced 734 axiom-audit occurrences across four source instances; all 14 false Lean claims failed logically. Source/reference/tamper checks reject 38 controls, and another 38 fully rehashed scope changes fail before archive extraction. Installed-wheel verification and recheck pass outside the checkout.\n\nLean 4.19.0 and nine locked Mathlib dependency sources/caches are required. The original Git dependency lock is retained. See reproduction/production_awq_gemm/REAL.md at the target source commit for commands, trust assumptions and immutable evidence.\n\nSHA256: c473e80dd1ee9b6cba4160371c5c06805ef771fbb165a6a4ddd6199925c6fd6d\n\nNo IEEE equality or floating-point error bound is claimed. This is the ninth independently accepted production family, not a reproduction of the authors' exact adapted PTX, original model/token experiments or NVIDIA measurements. No model calls or GPU launches were made by this proof extension.\n"
